;; Keys newsroom reads by name, so they need not be exported in the shell
;; that starts it. Written here on first run, readable by its owner only;
;; newsroom won't start if anyone else can read it, so keep it chmod 600.
;;
;; Each entry is a key's name and its value. A setting names a key as
;; ${NAME} or with :api-key-env, and the built-in providers look for theirs
;; under DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, ZHIPU_API_KEY and OPENAI_API_KEY; web search uses
;; EXA_API_KEY. A variable set in the environment wins over the same name
;; here. This file is read once, at startup, and never written again.
;;
;; {"DEEPSEEK_API_KEY" "sk-..."
;;  "SLACK_BOT_TOKEN" "xoxb-..."}
{}
